[Music]  a baseball glove is basically an  addition to your hand that allows you to  trap the balls between the thumb and the  index finger in such a fashion that you  can make a great catch and throw it back  so the time I started playing baseball  I've been in love with something very  basic about it it's not about fads or  this or that about a rich heritage that  goes back over a hundred years  [Music]  I'm Rob story I'm the executive vice  president  I cut the ball gloves we make world  class ball gloves here in Nocona Texas  to build a fluff you're going to have to  have the right leather we use a number  of different letters such as kangaroo  cowhide buffalo even some caiman when  that comes into us we begin the grading  process we're looking for any blemishes  scars defects with a classic walnut Club  we're going to be using the leather that  we call walnut crunch it's very durable  but very easy to break in a lot of  players lock that because I can go out  to play catch immediately we introduced  the cutting knives or what we call  clickers basically big cookie cutters  we've got to take that leather and cut  it into about 25 different pieces we've  have somewhere about 2,000 cutting dies  while the leather still flap do what we  call hot stamping it will take other  pieces to the embroidery station where  we have six and seen ahead  that can help out four to five hundred  dollars today putting all that  information somewhere on the weather so  that the customers educated  [Music]  once that's done then it's time to  transition over to the stitching  department two or three of the pieces go  a different direction where they're made  into the web or the pocket of the log  another station will start the interior  lining this is the part that the hand  touches not only the palm lining that  the back fingers as well as three Center  pads inside start to welt those parts  together where we're adding a third  piece of material in between the scenes  setting a spine to the backs of the  fingers of the glove really at that  point again to see the glove come  together  the fingers are finally married to the  front and it becomes a ship once you've  closed a glog it's inside out literally  push the leather down and push the  inside back to the outside then it's  time to start shaping the glove and we  do that through a series of forms that  look like giant hands they're heated to  about 250 degrees Fahrenheit pulled  around and shaped with a mallet so that  all the welting and all the seams are  just perfectly aligned  [Music]  living in a small town like that kind of  Texas is a big part of who I am I think  the kind of bungalows  wouldn't necessarily work somewhere else  it's about the local people in the pride  the town itself is very much a part of  the final product I'm a fourth  generation family member in the company  and in the 1960s most baseball glove  manufacturers decided to take their  manufacturing offshore  my grandfather mob story didn't want to  do that he wanted to give employment to  the locals he made a decision at that  point that was very crucial to the long  term history of our company and that was  that we were going to be american-made  something that's been a part of  Americana for decades and decades but  they can't find anywhere else now in the  United States there are up to 40  different labor operations that go into  making a glove and so it's not just  sticking a piece of leather in a machine  more and more people are starting to  realize just because you can make it  cheap way somewhere else that doesn't  make it good you've got to put the very  best craftsmanship in  we think our history of 80 plus years of  doing that we've learned how to do it  leather it's one of the most interesting  materials known to man  the field is firmly wrapped around your  hand the subtle pop doesn't ball hits it  these characteristics four things that  make crafting and with this medium one  of the most enjoyable parts of my job  [Music]  after the forming marry the outside  shell with the inside line we're going  to be gluing some parts together so in  the inside liner take long strips of  tensile strength laces and start filling  120 holes in the glove cosmoline holds  the palm to the inside of the liner into  very heavy form of petroleum jelly it  looks a lot like peanut butter it's a  great adhesive we can open up into love  10 years later and that stuff still  sticky inside first the top fingers then  the bottom perimeter of the glove and  finally the web which usually kind of  gives the glove its character into one  finalized piece  [Music]  we will physically beat the palm of the  glove and that softens the glove shapes  and leather takes out all the wrinkles  and makes it just right  we take hot petroleum jelly and lanolin  and we spray that onto the gloves so  that we have a very uniform layer of oil  that starts to moisturize the leather  just like skin if left to its own design  will start to dry out and crack and  flaky if we bag we tag the glove seal it  up and get it ready to go out to the  market  even though it's evolved through the  years it's still very very personal to  each player that uses a glove I think to  our customers McCullough bought gloves  represent a product that is rich in  heritage at the top level of the game  and hopefully last for decades to come  [Music]  you  [Music]  you

